Yes, thanks Marc, that is the paper. Survey protocol can very across observations, and it accepts both truncated (max distance is finite) and unlimited (max is infinity) counts in DS.

Tyler: have a look at the cmulti2.fit function, that does the joint estimation. But as shown in the example, it is identical to the 2-step marginal estimation due to the models being orthogonal. The cmulti formula interface is user friendlier, that's why I was suggested that.

